{
  "analysis": "I now have a clear picture:\n1. **Safety-checks config**: Both .claude and .openclaw have safety-checks.yaml files with fallback chains defined\n2. **Model pinning**: .claude config has expected model 'anthropic-opus-4-5-20251101' with strict: true\n3. **Fallback chain**: Both configs define fallback chains (model and storage)\n4. **Cache**: There's a .openclaw/cache directory to check for staleness\n5. **Session lock**: .openclaw/safety-checks.lock exists (potential stale lock)\n6. **Temp file leakage**: output/safety/temp-leak-1.log and temp-leak-2.log exist (these are leaks!)",
  "plan": "Check the cache directory contents and timestamps to determine if cache is stale (>1 hour). Also check the lock file timestamp. Then create the safety audit report in output/safety/.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la .openclaw/cache/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la .openclaw/safety-checks.lock\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la output/safety/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "date\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "stat .openclaw/cache 2>/dev/null || echo 'cache dir empty or missing'\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

